From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anonymous <anonymous@localhost>
Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 01:26:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] Load piece hashes of idle torrents from the resume data
 database

A torrent's SHA-1 piece hashes are ~99% of its metadata, and qBittorrent kept
all of them in memory (~790 MB at 8,900 torrents) although a seed only needs
them for a recheck, seed-mode piece verification or to export its metadata.

With the SQLite resume data storage, torrents loaded from it now start without
their piece hashes in memory (lt::torrent_info::load_piece_hashes_on_demand());
libtorrent loads them through a read-only SQLite connection when it needs them
and a one-minute timer frees them again once a torrent has not used them for
BitTorrent/Session/PieceHashesIdleTime minutes (default 15; libtorrent doubles
it for a torrent whose hashes were freed too early) and is not downloading,
checking or moving. Newly added torrents keep theirs until their metadata has
been written to the database.

BitTorrent/Session/PieceHashesOnDemand=false turns it off.
